  "notes": [
    "Same current source and fixed camera; control changes only renderer import/adapter and diagnostic label. Both decode/bake the same assets and use the same workers, lighting, UI and route. Service workers blocked.",
    "Three measured trials per viewport per renderer; first route warms route-specific render caches, warm ranges use trials 1 and 2. Raw reports include all trials and samples. No statistical or universal FPS guarantee.",
    "RAF intervals are measured frame scheduling; GPU/CPU/call/triangle values are repeated published diagnostics at native cadence, summarized as observed medians, not independent frame timings.",
    "CPU4x and mobile viewport are host emulation, not physical-phone measurements.",
    "No phone average-frame-time speedup established; observed control/static ranges overlap. Detail continuity and queue-free reuse improve.",
    "Actual instance semantics differ: old control uses per-voxel instances; static uses whole-prop/transition instances. Compare equivalentCells for LOD budget. geometryBytes/instanceBytes are scoped counters, not total RAM/VRAM.",
    "Queue-only post-follow timings may observe stale bulk metrics at up to 500ms publication cadence and do not prove all transitions/GI fully settled.",
    "Old static-before8c and static-after-v1 retain the mixed-input camera race and are historical combined-change evidence, not isolated mesh baselines."
  ]
